‎## 2. Definition — Capability, Not Trait
‎
‎**Old framing (personality):**
‎Adaptability = flexible person, open-minded, resilient character
‎
‎**New framing (operating capability):**
‎
‎> **Adaptability is the capacity to change your response without abandoning your underlying purpose.**
‎
‎> **Adaptability = preserving the objective while changing the approach when reality changes.**
‎
‎**That distinction matters.**
‎
‎- You don't throw away invariant simply because surface changes
‎- You adapt method, not necessarily mission
‎- You preserve objective, change approach
‎
‎**Links:**
‎
‎- Rule #13: Command as invariant — capacity to issue meaningful command remains while tools evolve
‎- Rule #14: Choice as agency — capacity to choose anytime anywhere cannot be duplicated
‎- Both are invariants. Adaptability preserves invariants while changing surface.
‎
